<title>USA: Iowa-So Minn hogs-Thursday estimate 105,000-USDA.</title>
<headline>Iowa-So Minn hogs-Thursday estimate 105,000-USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Estimates for Iowa and southern Minnesota hog receipts for Thursday were 105,000 head, compared with the Thanksgiving Day holiday last week and 110,000 a year ago. Estimates include generally about 60 percent Carcass Base Hogs. Barrows and gilts were steady with midsession Wednesday. Trade and demand was moderate for light to moderate offerings.</p>
<p>				  Country		    Plants</p>
<p>US 1-3   46-49% Carcass Base Lean*</p>
<p>220-260 lbs	    55.50 -57.00	    56.50 -58.00</p>
<p>Liberal Volume	 56.00 -56.50	   57.00 -57.50</p>
<p>few			55.00		    56.00</p>
<p>US 1-3   46-49% Carcass Base Lean*</p>
<p>260-280 lbs	    53.50 -57.00	   54.00 -58.00</p>
<p>US 2-4   43-49% Carcass Base Lean</p>
<p>280-300 lbs	    50.00 -55.50	   50.50 -56.50</p>
<p>Sows:  steady to 3.00 lower.</p>
<p>US 1-3 300-450 lbs.  42.00 -45.00	   43.00 -46.00</p>
<p>450-500 lbs.	   44.00 -46.00	   45.00 -46.00</p>
<p>500 lbs. up	    48.00 -50.00	   48.00 -51.00</p>
<p>Note: Prices quoted represent sales of hogs averaging 73-74 pct carcass yields with mostly 1.00-1.25 inches of last rib backfat and 47-48 pct lean. Special considerations and grade premiums not reflected in base prices.</p>
